Ólafr heiti ek, my name is O.;
Úlfr hét maðr, there was a man, whose name was U.;
bœr heitir á Bakka (at búrfelli), there is a farm called B.;
~ (to be reckoned) frjáls maðr, hvers manns níðingr;

with dat. to promise (~ e-m e-u);
mantu, hverju þú hézt mér, do you remember what you promised me?
~ e-m hörðu, to threaten one;
Bárði var heitit meyjunni, the maid was promised to B.;

abode of the dead (gráta Baldr ór ~ju);
leysa höfuð sitt ór ~ju, to save oneself from death;
rasa í ~ina opna, to rush into open death;
liggja á ~jar þremi, to be on the verge of death;

to catch with the hand (hann kastaði heininni í lopt upp, en allir vildu ~);
to pick out or up (hann safnar mönnum til at ~ svínin);
~ e-t augum, to catch with the eyes;
~ til smátt ok stórt, to pick up small and great alike, look closely after;
~ gaman (skemtan) at e-u, to take a delight in (hann hendi skemtan at sögum ok kvæðum);
~ sakir á e-m, to pick up charges against one;

with preps.:
~ af, here from, from this;
~ eptir, hereafter, according to this;
~ fyrir, for this, therefore;
~ til, hereto;
~ um, in this, as regards this.

to hear;
