~ illa, hard of hearing;
~ e-t til e-s, to hear (a sound) from one;
hefir hvárki heyrt til hans styn né hosta, neither groan nor cough has been heard from him;
heyrir blástr (acc.) hans í alla heima, when he blows, it can he heard in all the worlds;

to hit upon, meet with one;
~ ráð, to hit upon a device;
~ leiðina, to find one’s way;
absol., ~ inn í váginn, to find the way into the bay;
sjaldan hittir leiðr í lið, an unwelcome guest always misses the feast;
~ í vandræði, to get into scrapes;
~ á e-t, to hit upon (hitti hann þar á þórolf);

by, near;
liggja (sitja) ~ e-m, to lie (sit) by one;
sofa (hvíla) hjá e-m, to sleep with one;
~ durunum, near (close to) the door;

by, with;
vera ~ e-m, to stay with one;
vera í gistingu ~ e-m, to lodge with one;
maðr einn var eptir ~ honum, was left with him;

past, by;
fara, ganga ~ e-m, to go by, pass one (mánaði síðarr fóru þeir ~ mér kátir);
farast ~, to pass by one another;
fara ~ sér, to go beside oneself;
fram ~ Knafahólum, past K.;
þeir riðu ~ fram, they rode by;

to leap, jump (hann hljóp meirr en hæð sina);
