to listen (eyrum hlýðir hann, en augum skoðar);
~ e-m, to listen (give ear) to one;
~ messu, tíðum, to hear mass, attend service;
~ á e-t or til e-s, to listen to (sitja menn þar umhverfis ok ~ til sögunnar);

to do, be permissible or proper;
hlýðir það hvergi (it will not do) at hafa eigi lög í landi;
engum öðrum skyldi þat ~, nobody else should dare to do so;
Einar lét engum ~ móti at mæla, E. would not hear of any one’s gainsaying;

to laugh;
~ hátt, to laugh loud;
~ at e-u, to laugh at;
þau tíðendi, er þeim hló hugr við, that gladdened their hearts;

 hollow, cavity, esp. cavity of the body;
ganga (hlaupa) á ~, to pierce to the inwards (of weapons);
hit efra ~, the cavity of the chest;
neðra ~, the stomach.

to turn (be turned) in a certain direction;
horfði upp eggin, the edge turned upwards;
suðr horfðu dyrr, the door looked south;
h. baki við e-m, to turn the back against one;
h. við e-m, to face one; fig. to set oneself against one (þeir er heldr höfðu við honum horft í sínum huga);

to look in a certain way, to have a certain appearance;
h. úvænt, to look unpromising (úvænt horfir um sættir);
hvárum horfir vænna, who is more likely to get the betler;
