horfir mjök í móti oss, matters look bad for us;
horfir til gamans mikils, there is a prospect of much entertainment;

abandoned, forsaken;
heillum ~, forsaken by luck;
sök ~, having lost the suit;
heraði ~, bereft of a dwelling in the district.

moderation, measure;
kunna ~, to show (observe) moderation;
þá er ~ á (or at), then it is all right;
at ~i, tolerably, moderately (jarl svarar þessu at ~i vel);
e-t gegnir ~i, it is fair;
vel er þessu til ~s mikils, this affair is well settled;
ór ~i, beyond measure;

to fall back, recoil, be repelled;
~ frá, to shrink back;
~ fyrir e-m, to give way before one (gekk konungr svá hart fram, at allt hrökk fyrir honum);
~ undan, to give way, draw back, retreat (hrukku Baglar þá undan);
~ við, to stand at bay, make a stand (verðr Sigvaldi nú við at ~);

mind;
í hug eða verki, in mind or act;
vera í hug e-m, to be in one’s mind;
koma e-m í hug, to come into one’s mind, occur to one;
leiða e-t hugum, to consider;
ganga (líða, hverfa) e-m ór hug, to pass out of one’s memory, to be forgotten;
