leggja hug á konu, to fall in love with a woman;
mér leikr ~ á e-u, I long (wish) for a thing;
e-m rennr ~ til e-s, to have affection for one;
mér er engi ~ á at selja hann, I have no mind to sell him;

foreboding;
svá segir mér ~ um, I forebode;
hann kvað sér illa hug sagt hafa (he had evil forebodings) um hennar gjaforð;
mér býðr ~ um e-t, I anticipate (eptir gekk mér þat, er mér bauð ~ um);
mér býðr e-t í hug, it enters my mind, I think;
gøra sér í hug, to imagine;

 house (leita nú um hvert h. á þeim bœ);
pl. the group of buildings on a farm, = bœr;
taka hús (pl.) á e-m, to take a person by surprise in his house;
at húsa baki, at the back of the houses.

with preps. and advs.:
~ af at gera e-t, to leave off doing a thing;
~ aptr, to turn back, return;
aptr hverfr lygi, þá er sönnu mœtir, a lie recoils before the truth;
~ at e-m, to throng around one (þá hurfu þegar at honum allir ok fögnuðu honum);
~ at e-u, to turn to, to adopt (~ at e-u ráði);
~ brott, to disappear;
~ eptir e-m, to follow one;
~ frá e-u, to turn away from;
gørðu-t far festa, áðr þeir frá hyrfi, they did not moor the boat before they turned away; to leave off (nú skal þar til taka, sem fyrr var frá horfit);
~ í sundr, to part;
~ til e-s, to turn (go) to one, or to a place (hlæjandi Guðrún hvarf til skemmu); esp. to go to one and take leave (Gunnar hverfr til allra manna, er hann er búinn); to fall to one’s lot, accrue to one (þótti stór heill til hans horfit hafa);
~ um e-t, to encircle, surround (~ um hodd goða);
~ undan e-m, to be withdrawn from, lost to one (hvarf ríki í Noregi undan Dana konungum);

with acc. to rest;
~ lið sitt, to let one’s troops rest;
~ sik, to take rest (þeir hvíldu sik þar ok eyki sína);
hvíldr, rested (þeir hafa mœdda hesta, en vér höfum alla hvílda);
refl., ~st = ~ sík;

~ e-m e-t, to intend a thing for one, to have in store for one (þóttist þann vita, at honum mundi slíkr kostr hugaðr);
~ e-m vel, to be well disposed towards a person;
~ e-u illa, to be ill pleased with;
ok munu þau vel ~ (they will be glad), er þau hafa akrinn;

with preps.:
~ af e-u, to leave off thinking about, forget or drop (~ af harmi, heimsku);
~ af um leitina, to give up the search;
~ at e-u, to attend to, mind, look at;
konungr hugði vandliga at manninum, the king looked closely at the man;
~ á e-t, to think of (~ á flótta);
ef hann á grið hygði, if he thought of any breach of faith;
~ fyrir e-u, to look to, take heed to (hygg nú svá fyrir hag þínum);
~ til e-s, to look forward to with pleasure, etc. (hversu hyggr þú til at deyja? gott hygg ek til bana míns);
~ um e-t, to think about a thing;
~ um með e-m, to deliberate with one about a thing;

(-ta, -tr), , ~ sik e-m, to court a person’s friendship, make friends with;
~ fyrir e-m, to recommend one;
refl., ~st e-n = ~ sik e-m;
~st e-n at, to pay homage to.

(-s, -ar),  heel;
hlaupa (fara, ganga) á hæla e-m, to follow at one’s heels;
hurð felir (lýkst) á hæla e-m, the door shuts (closes) upon one’s heels;
fara aptr á hæli, to return immediately;
hopa (fara) á hæl fyrir e-m, to retreat, recede before one.

head (höggva ~ af e-m);
láta e-n höfði skemmra, to behead one;
strjúka aldrei um frjálst ~, to be never free, never at ease;
skera e-m ~, to make a wry face at one;
heita í ~ e-m, to be called after a person;
hætta höfði, to risk one’s life;
leggja við ~ sitt, to stake one’s head;
fœra e-m ~ sitt, to surrender oneself to an enemy;
drepa niðr höfði, to droop the head;
þoku hóf af höfði, the fog lifted;
stíga yfir ~ e-m, to overcome one;
hlaða helium að höfði e-m, to leave one dead on the spot;
ganga milli bols ok ~s e-s or á e-m, to hew of one’s head, to kill outright;
senda e-n til ~s e-m, to send one to take another’s head;
leggja fé til ~s e-m, to set a price on one’s head;
leggjast e-t undir ~, to put aside, neglect (Þ. lagðist eigi þessa ferð undir ~);
vera höfði hærri, to be taller by a head;

to strike, smite (with a sharp weapon);
høggr sá, er hlífa skyldi, he strikes who ought to shield;
~ sverði (or með sverði), to strike with a sword;
~ e-n bana-högg, to give one his deathblow;

with preps.:
~ e-t af, to hew or cut off (~ af kampa ok skegg);
~ af fé, to kill (slaughter) cattle;
~ e-t af sér, to ward of;
~ eptir e-m, to cut at one, = ~ til e-s (hjá eptir honum með sverði);
~ í höfuð e-m, to give one a blow on the head;
~ e-t niðr, to cut down (var merki hans niðr höggvit);
to kill, butcher (I. hefir áðr niðr höggvit brœðr sína tvá);
~ e-t ór, to cut out;
fig. to make even, smooth (láta konung ok erkibisup ór ~ slíkar greinir);
~ e-t í sundr, to hew asunder;
~ til e-s, to strike (cut) at one, = ~ eptir e-m;
~ upp tré, to cut down a tree;
~ upp skip, to break a ship up;

hand;
taka hendi á e-u, to touch with the hand;
hafa e-t í hendi, to hold in the hand;
drepa hendi við e-u, to refuse;
halda hendi yfir e-m, to protect one;
taka e-n ~um, to seize, capture;
bera ~ fyrir höfuð sér, to defend oneself;
eiga hendr sínar at verja, to act in self defence;
láta e-t hendi firr, to let go out of one’s hands, to lose;
taka í ~ e-m, to join hands with one;
eiga e-t jöfnum ~um, to own in equal shares;
sverja sér af hendi, to forswear;
af hendi e-s, on one’s behalf, on the part of (af hendi landsmanna);
at hendi, as adv. in turn;
hverr at hendi, each in turn;
felast á hendi e-m, to be under one’s protection;
hvat er þér á ~um, what hast thou in hand?;
ef honum væri ekki á ~um, if he had nothing in hand, if his hands were free;
eiga e-t fyrir hendi (~um), to have in hand (duty, business, engagement);
vera í hendi, to be at hand, at one’s disposal;
hafa vel (illa) í ~um, to behave well (badly);
hafa e-t með ~um, to have in hand, manage, discharge;
hljóta e-t undan hendi e-s, from one, at one’s hand;
á ~, á hendr, against (lýsa vígi á ~ e-m);
snúa vanda á hendr e-m, to throw the responsibility on one;
fœrast e-t á hendr, to undertake;
ganga (drífa) á ~ e-m, to submit to one;
bjargast á sínar hendr, by one’s own handiwork;
selja, gefa, fá e-t í ~ (hendr) e-m, to give into one’s hands, hand over;
búa e-t í hendr e-m, to make it ready for one;
kalla til e-s í hendr e-m, to lay claim to a thing at the hands of another;
þá sömu nótt, er fór í ~, the following night;
veðr óx í ~, the wind rose higher and higher;
vera hœgt um ~, to be easy in hand;
til handa e-m, into one’s hands;
ganga til handa e-m, to put oneself in another’s hands, submit to him;
ef þat berr þér til handa, if it befalls thee;
þá skömrn kýs ek mér eigi til handa, I will not have that shame at my door;
biðja konu til handa e-m, on one’s behalf, for him;

hand, side;
á hœgri (vinstri) ~, on the right (left) hand, side;
á hvára ~, on either hand;
minnar (yðvarrar) handar, for my (your) part;

 a plunge into water, dive, diving;
fær hann annat ~ at öðru, he gets one plunge after another;
taka ~, to dive under water;
á ~, í ~, into water, under water;
hlaupa á ~, to plunge into water;
fara í ~, to go under water;
á ~i, í ~i, under water, diving;
of snow, lágu hestarnir á ~i í snjónum, the horses stuck deep in the snow;
standa á ~i to sink deep (øxin stóð á kafi).

with preps.:
~ at e-m, to call to one;
~ á e-n, to call to one (Flosi gekk þá at durum ok ~ði á Njál); to call on, invoke (~ði hann á guð ok hinn helga Ólaf);
~ á e-t, to lay claim to (Snækollr ~ði á bú nökkur þar í eyjunum);
~ eptir, to protest;
~ e-n eptir e-m, to call or name after;
~ til e-s, to call to, invoke (~ til guðs); to lay claim to, to claim, demand (Snorri ~ði þá til brynju sinnar);
~ til e-s við e-n, í hendr e-m, to claim a thing from one.

to search, explore (þeir könnuðu landit fyrir austan ána);
~ lið, to review, muster troops;
~ val, to search the field for slain;
~ e-t af, to find out, make out (ferr Brandr biskup norðr á Völlu ok ~r þat af, at);
~ til = ~ af (~ðist svá til, at);

to cast, throw, with dat. (Egill ~ði þegar niðr horninu);
~ akkerum, to cast anchor;
~ verplum, teningum, to throw with dice;
~ orðum á e-n, to address one;
refl., ~st orðum á, to exchange words;
~ kalls-yrðum at e-m, to throw taunts at one;
~ eign sinni á e-t, to seize upon, take possession of;
~ á sik sótt, to feign illness;

impers., e-u ~r, is thrown, flung;
tóku þeir gneista þá, er ~t hafði ór Múspellsheimi, they took the sparks that had been cast out from M.;
skipinu hafði ~t, had capsized;
henni var ~t skinni at beini, the skin was, as it were, thrown over her bones (from leanness);

bargain;
illt (gott) ~, bad (good) bargain;
slá ~i við e-n, to strike a bargain with one;
eiga ~ við e-n, to bargain, trade with one;
verða at ~i, to come to a bargain;

with preps.:
~ e-n á braut, to buy one of;
~ e-t at e-m, to buy a thing of one;
~ saman, to bargain;
~ um e-t, to barter, exchange (keypti hann um lönd við Guðrúnu);
~ við e-n, to make a bargain, come to terms with one;
recipr., ~st við, to bargain with one another.

to feel, perceive, with acc. and gen. (ek kennda þín eigi, er þú hvíldir á brjósti mér);
